Now, excuse me.

12:36.597 --> 12:38.764
(groans)

12:39.866 --> 12:42.835
You're standing on my leash.

12:46.873 --> 12:48.741
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:48.743 --> 12:51.110
♪ All the single Barrys,
all the single Barrys ♪

12:51.112 --> 12:52.778
♪ Make a turkey sandwich,
make a turkey sandwich ♪

12:52.780 --> 12:55.281
♪ If you like it then you should
have put some cheese on it ♪

12:55.283 --> 12:57.116
♪ If you like it then you should
have put some cheese on it ♪

12:57.118 --> 13:01.420
♪ May-a-o, oh-oh-oh,
oh-oh-oh, oh... ♪

13:01.422 --> 13:04.023
Oh, hey.

13:04.025 --> 13:06.359
Bare, can I talk to you?

13:06.361 --> 13:07.827
Sure. What's up?

13:07.829 --> 13:09.462
Let me ask you something.

13:09.464 --> 13:11.764
Suppose you had someone
living with you,

13:11.766 --> 13:14.233
and you wanted them to leave.

13:14.235 --> 13:16.736
How would you go about
making that clear?

13:16.738 --> 13:18.804
Well, I don't like
confrontation,

13:18.806 --> 13:20.573
so I'd probably do something
passive-aggressive

13:20.575 --> 13:21.907
like sit them down

13:21.909 --> 13:23.576
and ask them
how they would approach...

13:23.578 --> 13:25.611
Oh, you're asking me
to move out.

13:25.613 --> 13:28.381
No, no, no, no, I'm not
asking you to move out.

13:28.383 --> 13:32.251
I'm-I'm asking you
to move in...

13:32.253 --> 13:34.787
to the... outside.

13:34.789 --> 13:36.989
Okay.

13:36.991 --> 13:38.691
Boy, man, I'm so sorry.

13:38.693 --> 13:41.060
I just have been having a lot
of fun here, you know.

13:41.062 --> 13:43.396
Everybody's so nice,
and you've been so welcoming.

13:43.398 --> 13:46.132
Up until just now when you
told me to get the hell out.

13:46.134 --> 13:47.299
Don't get me wrong.

13:47.301 --> 13:49.201
It's not that I don't love
having you here.

13:49.203 --> 13:51.637
It's just that I don't think
that I can legally

13:51.639 --> 13:54.573
have anyone else live here
unless I adopt them.

13:54.575 --> 13:56.942
I'm down for that.

13:56.944 --> 13:59.011
Okay, well, let's table that,

13:59.013 --> 14:03.115
but in-in the meantime, we'll
look for an apartment for you.

14:03.117 --> 14:06.218
Uh, well, I mean,
today is kind of already shot.

14:06.220 --> 14:07.920
Maybe pick it up tomorrow?

14:07.922 --> 14:09.855
Yeah. Okay, yeah.

14:09.857 --> 14:12.625
I mean, it's-it's 10:30.

14:12.627 --> 14:16.495
In the morning.

14:16.497 --> 14:18.464
Great.
Uh, I'm gonna go get high

14:18.466 --> 14:20.132
and eat my sandwich
out on the deck.

14:20.134 --> 14:22.301
Okay

14:25.038 --> 14:27.273
He's never moving out.

14:27.275 --> 14:29.341
Hey.
Oh, hey.

14:29.343 --> 14:32.945
Wait. Are you just getting back
from your date with Gretchen?

14:32.947 --> 14:35.314
No. No, no. I had to go back
to the restaurant.

14:35.316 --> 14:37.116
I left my hat
at the valet stand.

14:37.118 --> 14:38.250
Liar!

14:39.753 --> 14:41.687
You would never pay for parking.

14:42.856 --> 14:45.124
All right, admit it,
you slept with Gretchen.

14:45.126 --> 14:47.460
You're right, I slept with her.

14:47.462 --> 14:50.696
And I found a broken meter
two blocks from the restaurant.

14:50.698 --> 14:52.498
I thought you were
calling it off with her.

14:52.500 --> 14:55.301
Well, I started to, but
you-you know how breakups go.

14:55.303 --> 14:57.236
I mean, you try
to be considerate

14:57.238 --> 14:59.705
and let her down easy,
and next thing you know,

14:59.707 --> 15:01.707
you're wearing a dog collar
and a leash

15:01.709 --> 15:04.777
while she lets you
lick peanut butter

15:04.779 --> 15:07.279
out of a chew toy
between her boobs.

15:09.049 --> 15:12.384
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:12.386 --> 15:14.787
Whoa...

15:14.789 --> 15:16.789
Look at this place.

15:16.791 --> 15:20.059
Hello, apartment,
good-bye panties, huh?

15:20.061 --> 15:22.127
I don't think
this place is for me.

15:22.129 --> 15:24.630
It just doesn't scream "Barry."

15:24.632 --> 15:27.399
It will
when the panties come off.

15:27.401 --> 15:29.435
No. Plus, the feng shui
is just off.

15:29.437 --> 15:30.703
All right.

15:30.705 --> 15:32.438
This is the sixth place
you didn't like.

15:32.440 --> 15:35.975
And the last one you said was
in a bad school district.

15:37.344 --> 15:38.611
What's going on here?

15:38.613 --> 15:41.213
Nothing. Nothing's
going on. I just...

15:41.215 --> 15:43.349
I've never really
lived alone before.

15:43.351 --> 15:44.517
Never?

15:44.519 --> 15:46.819
Well, when my dad left,
I lived with my mom,

15:46.821 --> 15:48.354
and then boarding school,

15:48.356 --> 15:50.022
and then, in college,
I always had roommates,

15:50.024 --> 15:51.924
and then after college,
I lived with Nicole.

15:51.926 --> 15:53.659
I mean,
I'm like a baby duck, Walden.

15:53.661 --> 15:56.695
When Mama Duck leaves, I cling
to the next mama duck.

15:56.697 --> 15:59.298
Okay, but my flock is too big,

15:59.300 --> 16:03.736
so, you gotta get the flock
out of my house.

16:03.738 --> 16:05.371
I don't know
if I can make it on my own.

16:05.373 --> 16:06.805
Okay, listen, I know
what's going on.

16:06.807 --> 16:07.973
I know how you feel.

16:07.975 --> 16:10.042
I felt the same way when
my wife walked out on me.

16:10.044 --> 16:11.110
What did you do?

16:11.112 --> 16:12.545
I bought a house

16:12.547 --> 16:16.282
and let a 45-year-old man
and his son live there.

16:16.284 --> 16:18.717
Wow. A real
&lt;i>Scared Straight&lt;/i> moment here.

16:18.719 --> 16:20.619
Let's grab up a pizza
on the way back to the beach.

16:20.621 --> 16:21.754
Barry, listen to me.

16:21.756 --> 16:23.188
I'm going to say
something to you

16:23.190 --> 16:25.257
that I have never
said before in my life.

16:25.259 --> 16:27.226
You can't live with me.

16:27.228 --> 16:28.694
Oh, my God.

16:28.696 --> 16:31.931
(laughing)

16:31.933 --> 16:33.933
I did it.

16:33.935 --> 16:35.668
I'm sorry.
You're-You're my first.

16:35.670 --> 16:37.136
No, no, no,
I don't want to be your first.

16:37.138 --> 16:38.604
Your first should be
someone special,

16:38.606 --> 16:41.173
like a whore
that your stepdad buys you.

16:42.576 --> 16:44.643
...is an example I just made up.

16:44.645 --> 16:47.746
Listen, Barry, you're...
you are gonna be okay.

16:47.748 --> 16:50.649
And you can come and visit
anytime that you want.

16:50.651 --> 16:51.417
Really?

16:51.419 --> 16:53.218
Yeah, just stop on by.

16:53.220 --> 16:55.087
But you can't live with me!

16:55.089 --> 16:56.855
Now or ever.

16:56.857 --> 16:58.757
Okay, but I can't just
stay here.

16:58.759 --> 16:59.959
Yes, you can!

16:59.961 --> 17:01.627
I'm gonna take care
of the paperwork,

17:01.629 --> 17:03.429
and then
I'll send your stuff over.

17:03.431 --> 17:04.830
You just make yourself at home.

17:04.832 --> 17:06.365
But you can't live with me!

17:06.367 --> 17:08.834
All right, message received.

17:08.836 --> 17:10.569
Okay, I'm sorry--
I'm just... I'm really excited.

17:10.571 --> 17:12.037
This is a big moment for me.

17:12.039 --> 17:14.139
I'm gonna go find Alan.

17:14.141 --> 17:15.574
You can't live with me!

17:17.110 --> 17:18.344
You can't live with me!

17:18.346 --> 17:19.311
Oh, I'm sorry, sir.

17:19.313 --> 17:20.446
But you can't
live with me!

17:20.448 --> 17:21.880
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

17:21.882 --> 17:25.150
I can't tell you how happy I am
you guys are dating.

17:25.152 --> 17:26.752
(laughs)

17:26.754 --> 17:28.954
No offense, Sis, but some of
the guys you've brought home--

17:28.956 --> 17:31.323
I mean, no job,
no house, no car.

17:31.325 --> 17:32.758
Real losers.

17:34.494 --> 17:36.028
Wow, sounds like the deadbeats

17:36.030 --> 17:38.063
I used to date
before I found Larry.

17:38.065 --> 17:41.634
Well, I've, uh, I've had some
real winners in my past, too.

17:41.636 --> 17:43.068
Cheaters, drunks,

17:43.070 --> 17:46.271
45-year-old women
trying to pass as 38.

17:46.273 --> 17:48.741
Lyndsey just turned 38!

17:49.876 --> 17:53.278
Well, luckily, those people
are out of our lives now.

17:53.280 --> 17:55.214
Yeah, but sometimes I swear

17:55.216 --> 17:57.783
I can see their stupid faces
right in front of me.

17:57.785 --> 18:01.020
That might be
a wine-induced hallucination.

18:01.022 --> 18:03.656
Speaking of wine,
a toast to the four of us.

18:03.658 --> 18:06.592
May this be the first
of many dinners, celebrations,

18:06.594 --> 18:08.727
holidays, vacations,
anniversaries...

18:08.729 --> 18:11.163
Yeah, yeah,
yeah, we get it.

18:11.165 --> 18:13.365
To us. Bottoms up.
(Alan chuckles)

18:13.367 --> 18:14.600
I know mine will be.

18:14.602 --> 18:17.302
Mmm! You are a bad girl.
(chuckles)

18:17.304 --> 18:19.405
(clears her throat)

18:19.407 --> 18:22.374
I think we're making
them uncomfortable.

18:22.376 --> 18:24.243
Not as uncomfortable
as last night,

18:24.245 --> 18:27.212
having sex with your butt
on a hot stove.

18:27.214 --> 18:28.614
We were fooling
around in the kitchen,

18:28.616 --> 18:30.716
and I picked him up
in a moment of passion.

18:30.718 --> 18:32.051
(laughs)

18:33.319 --> 18:35.220
I loved it.

18:36.322 --> 18:38.157
LARRY:
Wow!

18:38.159 --> 18:40.993
Lyndsey doesn't use the stove
for cooking or sex.

18:43.697 --> 18:45.998
Sweetie, sweetie,
what are you doing?

18:46.000 --> 18:48.133
Don't forget the little butter packets.
Oh!

18:49.536 --> 18:50.669
You're my little butter packet.

18:50.671 --> 18:51.704
Oh.

18:51.706 --> 18:53.238
(chuckles)

18:53.240 --> 18:54.306
Doesn't look
like they're thinking

18:54.308 --> 18:55.808
about any of their exes now.

18:55.810 --> 18:57.710
No, it doesn't.

18:57.712 --> 18:58.977
He's thinking
about banging my sister.

18:58.979 --> 19:00.679
I know what he's thinking!

19:02.882 --> 19:04.416
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:04.418 --> 19:07.453
Okay.

19:07.455 --> 19:09.688
One roommate down,
two to go.

19:09.690 --> 19:10.689
Alan...

19:10.691 --> 19:12.458
Hey, there he is.

19:12.460 --> 19:14.226
Barry?

19:14.228 --> 19:15.761
What are you doing here?

19:15.763 --> 19:19.031
Well, you said I could stop
by anytime I wanted, so...

19:19.033 --> 19:21.133
Yeah, but I-I just left you.

19:21.135 --> 19:23.469
17 minutes ago.

19:23.471 --> 19:25.404
I know.
I missed you, too.

19:26.506 --> 19:28.073
Walden, are you done?
We're in the middle of a game.

19:28.075 --> 19:29.708
Hey, can you go
on a beer run?

19:29.710 --> 19:31.410
What the hell is going on here?

19:31.412 --> 19:33.011
This is my house!

19:33.013 --> 19:34.713
BERTA:
Do you mind?!

19:34.715 --> 19:38.283
Some of us are trying to nap!

19:38.285 --> 19:41.186
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:41.188 --> 19:43.288
Oh, oh, well, then put up
a sign that says

19:43.290 --> 19:46.725
only one roll of mints
per customer.

19:46.727 --> 19:47.993
(door closes)

19:47.995 --> 19:49.061
Oh.

19:49.063 --> 19:50.229
Lyndsey.

19:51.431 --> 19:52.664
Are you waiting?

19:52.666 --> 19:54.967
Someone pooping in there?

19:54.969 --> 19:57.035
What the hell was that about?

19:57.037 --> 19:59.138
(imitating Gretchen): "You're my
little butter packet."

19:59.140 --> 20:00.305
What upset you more?

20:00.307 --> 20:01.507
That she stole that bread...

20:01.509 --> 20:03.408
or my heart?

20:03.410 --> 20:05.244
So you are doing this
just to make me jealous.

20:05.246 --> 20:06.545
No, that's not it at all.

20:06.547 --> 20:08.547
Too bad, 'cause it's working.

20:09.582 --> 20:10.916
I'm sorry, I...

20:10.918 --> 20:12.050
No, I-I really like Gretchen.

20:12.052 --> 20:13.085
I-I can't do this.

20:13.087 --> 20:14.686
Jeff Strongman can't.

20:14.688 --> 20:16.622
But Alan Harper can.

20:16.624 --> 20:18.457
Works for me.

20:18.459 --> 20:21.260
(both moaning)

20:21.262 --> 20:22.661
Is that a roll of mints
in your pocket

20:22.663 --> 20:24.196
or are you just
happy to see me?

20:24.198 --> 20:27.166
Actually,
it is a roll of mints.

20:27.168 --> 20:29.902
And a comb.

20:29.904 --> 20:32.471
And a bottle of Paco Rabanne.

20:32.473 --> 20:35.140
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:41.296 --> 20:42.563
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:42.565 --> 20:45.199
All right, the shot
for the win.

20:45.201 --> 20:47.601
Be the ball, see the cups.

20:47.603 --> 20:49.169
Hey, Barry, check
out these cups.

20:50.472 --> 20:52.473
Aah! Ball to the face.

20:52.475 --> 20:54.208
First time for everything.

20:55.110 --> 20:57.945
I may need to see that
again and again.

20:57.947 --> 20:59.980
Walden, we have
security cameras, right?

21:01.149 --> 21:02.316
Where's Walden?

21:03.651 --> 21:05.652
(music soundtrack playing on TV)

21:05.654 --> 21:07.354
I could totally live here.

21:08.841 --> 21:11.600
(laughs)
Screech, will you never learn?

21:11.601 --> 21:16.601
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
